      "math_academy_id": "q-36586",
      "sequence_position": 9,
      "problem": "The table below defines the function $f(x).$ Given that $f(x)$ is an even function, find the value of $a+b.$\n\n| **$x$** | $-123$ | $-71$ | $-29$ | $29$ | $71$ | $123$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $8$ | $a+12$ | $-4$ | $-4$ | $20$ | $b-2$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Since $f(x)$ is an even function, we must have that $f(-x)=f(x).$ \n\nUsing the fact that $f(-71)=f(71),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-71) & =f(71) \\\\ a+12 & =20 \\\\ a & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $f(-123)=f(123),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-123) & =f(123) \\\\ 8 & =b-2 \\\\ 10 & =b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\na+b=8+10=18.\n$$",
